{
  "id": "tactile-extinction",
  "term": "tactile extinction",
  "definition": "Tactile extinction is a problem seen after unilateral brain damage in which a person may miss a touch on the side opposite the lesion, especially when a touch is given at the same time on the same-side limb. It reflects a higher-order disturbance of spatial attention or representation rather than simply loss of basic touch sensation.",
  "field": "learning",
